.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
logs/
*.log
.telegram_offset
token.json

# Scene Planner V2 cardinality-mismatch diagnostic (TEMPORARY - see
# _write_cardinality_diagnostic() in youtube/scene_planner.py). Local-only
# debug output, never meant to be committed.
debug_audit/

# YouTube OAuth credential files (Round 3.2 multi-channel): this project's
# own config (core/config.py, youtube/uploader.py) reads OAuth client
# id/secret/refresh-token values from environment variables only - never
# from a JSON file - but the Google Cloud Console OAuth-client download is
# still commonly saved locally as client_secret*.json (or per-channel,
# e.g. youtube/client_secret_english.json) for reference while copying
# values into .env. These patterns keep any such file - and any ad hoc
# per-channel token/credential file someone adds later - out of git,
# wherever in the repo it's placed.
client_secret*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*_token.json
credentials/
youtube/credentials/

# Generated per-video output (research.json/script.json/scenes.json/
# scene_*.png/narration.mp3/video.mp4/.../state.json under
# storage/<year>/<month>/<slug>/) and the runtime SQLite DB - NOT the
# storage/ Python package that lives in this same directory
# (storage/__init__.py, db.py, project_store.py). A blanket "storage/"
# rule here would also silently gitignore those source files - confirmed
# with `git check-ignore -v storage/db.py` - and the "!storage/..."
# negation pattern that used to try to carve them back out never actually
# worked, since git cannot re-include a path inside an already-excluded
# parent directory. Ignoring only the specific runtime-generated paths
# avoids both problems.
storage/factory.db
storage/20[0-9][0-9]/
storage/music/*
!storage/music/.gitkeep
